In article <1993Feb27.222537.22833@leland.Stanford.EDU> trump@leland.Stanford.EDU (Michael Jason Lewis) writes:
>If you can't figure out the question from the subject, you probably don't know
>the answer...
>(there's no command line in Mac to start the game, so what do I do?)

     When the game asks "Who are you?" at the start of the game, just answer
"wizard".  Then it doesn't matter what character class you choose; you should
be in wizard mode.
     (Note that, at least on my copy, putting "wizard" in as your name in the
NetHack options file doesn't work; you have to delete any name you've put in
the options file, start the game, let the "who are you?" dialog pop up, and
put in "wizard" there.)
